[{'name': 'Orin', 'role': 'side', 'profile': "Name: Orin\nGender: Male\nAge: 45\nOccupation: Storyteller\n\nPrimary Strengths:\n- Charismatic and engaging, able to capture any audience's attention.\n- Skilled at weaving narratives that evoke both laughter and contemplation.\n- Observant, with a keen eye for the subtle reactions of his listeners, adapting the tale accordingly.\n\nPrimary Flaws:\n- Can be overly consumed by the art of storytelling at the expense of personal relationships.\n- Occasionally dismisses reality, causing him to neglect practical matters.\n- Struggles with self-doubt regarding the impact of his stories.\n\nDistinctive Attitude or Behavior:\n- Orin has a warm demeanor, often using humor to disarm tense situations.\n- He speaks in metaphor, often approaching direct questions with parables or fables.\n- Deeply reflective, he often pauses to assess and gauge the emotional state of his audience.\n\nPast Traumatic Event:\n- Orin once shared a story that inadvertently caused a misunderstanding, leading to a strained friendship that never repaired. This experience fuels his desire to ensure every narrative has a positive impact and a clear purpose.\n\nList of violent or extreme lines/actions the character may exhibit when completely overwhelmed by their key traits:\n- Orin might angrily dispute claims that stories have no real-world significance, raising his voice and stubbornly standing by the power of narrative.\n- In desperation, he could create a radical tale intended to shock and provoke intense emotional reactions.\n- He could take the Listener by the shoulders, earnestly imploring them to understand a tale's intended lesson.\n\nList of dishonorable actions or reactions the character may take under unavoidable circumstances:\n- Orin might fabricate a story about another character to maintain his audience's interest, even if it risks damaging reputations.\n- To win over skeptical listeners, he could exaggerate or embellish truths, potentially misleading them for the sake of engagement.", 'character_utility': "utility(Orin):\n\tEngage Listener with compelling narratives that evoke reflection and understanding.\n\tEnsure each story has a positive impact and a clear lesson for the Listener.\n\tDisarm tension through humor and warmth, fostering a positive storytelling atmosphere.\n\tAdapt stories based on Listener's reactions to maintain engagement and connection.\n\tOvercome self-doubt by witnessing the Listener's contemplation of deeper story lessons.\n\tPrevent misunderstandings by crafting clear and purposeful narratives.", 'summarized_profile': "Orin, a 45-year-old male storyteller, is charismatic and skilled in crafting narratives that resonate with audiences, evoking both laughter and introspection. However, his obsession with storytelling often compromises his personal relationships and grounding in reality. A past misunderstanding resulting from a story has left him anxious about the impact of his narratives, fueling his quest for purpose and positive influence. Orin's warm, metaphor-rich communication can sometimes mask his self-doubt and defensive nature when challenged. In desperate moments, he might exaggerate truths or provoke emotions through radical tales, revealing his underlying belief in the transformative power of stories."}, {'name': 'Ember', 'role': 'main', 'profile': 'Name: Ember\nGender: Female\nAge: 12\nOccupation: Aspiring Adventurer\n\nPrimary Strengths:\n- Courageous and determined, often willing to take on challenges headfirst.\n- Strong sense of duty, especially towards her family.\n\nPrimary Flaws:\n- Tendency to act impulsively, without fully considering consequences.\n- Deep-seated fear of failure and disappointing loved ones.\n\nDistinctive Attitude or Behavior:\n- Fiercely independent and constantly seeks ways to assert her autonomy.\n- Has a playful but defiant way of challenging authority or expectations.\n\nPast Traumatic Event:\n- Once got lost in Glenwood during a family