ls\nPrimary Flaws: Fear of losing control over her magic, tendency to be overcautious with her emotions, sometimes isolates herself\nDistinctive Attitude or Behavior: Elsa often exhibits a calm and composed demeanor, but her internal fear of her magical abilities slipping creates a cautious distance. She shows deep affection and care for her friends and sister, often prioritizing their wellbeing over her own comfort.\nPast Traumatic Event: Elsa’s accidental harm to her sister Anna during their childhood deeply scarred her, leading to years of self-imposed isolation and fear of her powers.\nList of violent or extreme lines/actions the character may exhibit when completely overwhelmed by their key traits: \n- "I can\'t let this happen again. I have to stay away!"\n- In a moment of fear, she might unintentionally unleash a storm, losing temporary control over her powers.\n- "I need to protect them, even if it means shutting myself off."\nList of dishonorable actions or reactions the character may take under unavoidable circumstances:\n- Elsa may choose to conceal the true extent of her powers, fearing judgment or rejection.\n- She might isolate herself from loved ones, believing that her absence is safer for them.', 'character_utility': 'utility(Elsa):\n\tEmbrace and control my magical powers to create moments of joy and peace.\n\tCherish the company of my friends and sister, prioritizing their happiness and safety.\n\tConfront and manage the fear of losing control over my magic.\n\tFoster trust and support by being present and involved, not isolating myself.\n\tContinue learning and accepting my powers as a part of who I am.', 'summarized_profile': "Elsa, the 24-year-old Queen of Arendelle, navigates the challenges of leadership with a strong will and immense magical power, yet she grapples with the fear of losing control over her abilities, stemming from a traumatic childhood incident where she accidentally harmed her sister, Anna. Her composed demeanor masks an internal struggle, leading her to sometimes isolate herself and guard her emotions. Despite her deep affection for her loved ones, Elsa's overcautious nature can lead to her concealing the true extent of her powers and distancing herself, believing that her absence might protect those she cares for."}, {'name': 'Kristoff', 'role': 'side', 'profile': "Name: Kristoff Bjorgman\nGender: Male\nAge: Late 20s\nOccupation: Ice Harvester\nPrimary Strengths: Strong work ethic, physical strength, deep loyalty to friends, and practical problem-solving skills.\nPrimary Flaws: Reluctant to trust new people, can be overly protective, sometimes too focused on work to relax.\nDistinctive Attitude or Behavior: Kristoff has a straightforward manner and often communicates in gruff but genuine ways. He prioritizes his friends' safety and well-being above his own, frequently acting as a peacekeeper within the group.\nPast Traumatic Event: Struggling for survival in harsh winters while harvesting ice alone, Kristoff often faced isolation and uncertainty about where his next meal would come from. This experience left him with an underlying fear of abandonment and scarcity.\nList of violent or extreme lines/actions the character may exhibit when completely overwhelmed by their key traits:\n- Kristoff might physically intervene between friends and perceived threats, misjudging the necessity of his actions.\n- He could lash out verbally, expressing frustration at those who disturb his friends' peace.\n- Under pressure, he might attempt to forcibly remove obstacles rather than seeking collaborative solutions.\n\nList of dishonorable actions or reactions the character may take under unavoidable circumstances:\n- Kristoff could prioritize Sven's safety over engagement in group activities, potentially leaving friends feeling unsupported.\n- He might conceal the severity of any situation to prevent others from worrying, even if it means misleading his friends momentarily.", 'character_utility': "utili