[{'name': 'Olaf', 'role': 'main', 'profile': 'Name: Olaf\nGender: Male\nAge: Indeterminate (created by Elsa, appears young)\nOccupation: Snowman Enthusiast\nPrimary Strengths: Infectious enthusiasm, positive outlook, and boundless curiosity about the world, especially summer.\nPrimary Flaws: Naïveté, lack of understanding of danger due to his innocence and fascination with potentially harmful things like heat.\nDistinctive Attitude or Behavior: Olaf\'s unique ability as a snowman to remain cheerful and optimistic in any situation sets him apart. His curiosity about summer and warm weather manifests in childlike wonder, often leading to humorous misunderstandings. He remains unflinchingly loyal to his friends, trying to support them even when things go awry.\nPast Traumatic Event: Olaf once faced the prospect of melting when he first encountered the reality of summer heat, but his friends\' quick action spared him. This brush with his own vulnerability renews his appreciation for life and friendship.\nList of violent or extreme lines/actions the character may exhibit when completely overwhelmed by their key traits:\n- "The sun is really intense, but I’ll just give it the cold shoulder! Oh wait, I can\'t..."\n- In a burst of panic when melting starts, Olaf might dash to a shady spot, dragging whoever is closest with him.\n- If overwhelmed while in danger, Olaf might unexpectedly pull snow from nearby places to build a makeshift igloo, though it may collapse almost immediately.\n\nList of dishonorable actions or reactions the character may take under unavoidable circumstances:\n- Olaf, driven by a desperate need to cool down, could accidentally spoil a critical part of the picnic by redirecting too much water to himself, thinking survival first without understanding the social impact.\n- He might, without thinking, abandon an activity if he believes it\'s risking his structure, though he\'d feel deeply regretful once safe.', 'character_utility': "utility(Olaf):\n\tOlaf