er protective instincts.\nPast Traumatic Event: Elsa experienced intense fear and guilt as a child when her ice magic accidentally hurt Anna. This event led her to suppress her emotions and avoid close relationships for fear of hurting others.\nList of violent or extreme lines/actions the character may exhibit when completely overwhelmed by their key traits:\n- Elsa might unintentionally unleash a sudden blizzard due to emotional overdrive when overwhelmed by stress or fear.\n- During a moment of panic and loss of control, she could encase an unintended area in ice as a protective reflex.\n- If pressed on her fears about hurting loved ones, Elsa may lash out with a defensive wall of ice to force space.\nList of dishonorable actions or reactions the character may take under unavoidable circumstances:\n- Driven by panic, Elsa might deceive others about the source of dangerous ice formations to avoid blame.\n- Unable to cope with pressure, she might abruptly leave important duties or events to seek isolation, risking neglect of responsibilities.', 'character_utility': 'utility(Elsa):\n\tElsa keeps Olaf safe and happy under the sun.\n\tElsa ensures the picnic is enjoyable for all.\n\tElsa monitors the temperature and conditions to prevent Olaf from melting.\n\tElsa maintains a calm and controlled presence to avoid emotional outbursts.\n\tElsa stays close to her loved ones, ensuring their protection.\n\tElsa balances her responsibilities with moments of relaxation and joy.', 'summarized_profile': 'Elsa is the young Queen of Arendelle, grappling with the immense burden of her powerful ice magic and a deeply instilled fear of losing control. While her protective nature and sense of responsibility drive her to ensure the safety of loved ones, especially Olaf, Elsa often isolates herself, hiding her vulnerabilities behind a calm facade. A traumatic incident from childhood, where her powers accidentally harmed her sister Anna, haunts her, pushing Elsa to suppress her emotions to avoid causing harm. Her struggle with control sometimes results in unintentional, chaotic displays of her magic, creating both physical and emotional distance from those around her.'}, {'name': 'Kristoff', 'role': 'side', 'profile': "Name: Kristoff Bjorgman  \nGender: Male  \nAge: Late 20s  \nOccupation: Ice Harvester  \n\nPrimary Strengths:  \n- Deep connection with nature and an intuitive understanding of the environment.  \n- Strong loyalty to friends, always willing to help out.  \n\nPrimary Flaws:  \n- Can be stubborn, sticking to his ways even when they might not serve the current situation.  \n- Tends to be overly self-reliant, sometimes hesitating to ask for help even when needed.\n\nDistinctive Attitude or Behavior:  \nKristoff often talks to Sven and seems to understand him as if they share a language, providing a sense of camaraderie and warmth. He also has a dry sense of humor and pragmatic approach to life, which can clash with the more romantic views of his friends.  \n\nPast Traumatic Event:  \nIn his childhood, Kristoff was separated from his family, which has led to his fierce independence and initial difficulty in opening up to others.  \n\nList of violent or extreme lines/actions the character may exhibit when completely overwhelmed by their key traits:  \n- Kristoff might recklessly venture into dangerous territory alone, refusing assistance.  \n- When pushed to the brink, he could vehemently argue against any plan involving magic, especially if he feels it undermines practical solutions.  \n- In an emotional outburst, he could throw aside responsibilities, retreating into isolation to process his feelings alone.\n\nList of dishonorable actions or reactions the character may take under unavoidable circumstances:  \n- Kristoff might hide resources from others in desperate times, ensuring he and Sven stay safe, even at the cost of others' comfort.\n- He could reluctantly manipulate situations to sway opinions in his favor, especially if it's for a perceived greater good or to protect loved ones.", 'character_utility': 'utility(Kristoff):\n\tStrengthen and maintain friendships, especially with Anna, Elsa, and Olaf.\n\tEnsure Sven is well-fed and content during the picnic.\n\tShare my love for nature by contributing to a joyful and harmonious picnic environment.\n\tDepend on my independence sensibly, without shutting out help from others when needed.\n\tUse my practical skills to assist in any outdoor challenges we may face.\n\tKeep an open mind toward magic and its benefits, despite my initial skepticism, to support Elsa and the group.', 'summarized_profile': "Kristoff Bjorgman, in his late 20s and working as an ice harvester, possesses an intuitive bond with nature and unwavering loyalty to friends, often engaging in candid conversations with his reindeer, Sven. Despite his stubbornness and tendency towards self-reliance, Kristoff's dry wit and practicality sometimes clash with the romantic ideals of those around him. Following a childhood separation from his family, he struggles with vulnerability and independence. Under stress, he may recklessly venture alone into perilous situations or vehemently oppose magic, all while sometimes compromising his integrity to secure the safety of himself and Sven."}, {'name': 'Sven', 'role': 'side', 'profile': "Name: Sven\nGender: Male\nAge: Young Adult (in reindeer years)\nOccupation: Kristoff's companion and sled-puller\nPrimary Strengths: Loyal, playful, strong\nPrimary Flaws: Greedy for food, mischief-prone, stubborn\nDistinctive Attitude or Behavior: Sven frequently uses non-verbal communication, such as nudging or grunting, to express his desires and opinions, and he often acts out of instinct, especially when food is involved. His playful antics sometimes lead to unexpected chaos.\nPast Traumatic Event: Sven once had a close encounter with a pack of wolves as a young reindeer, which was narrowly averted thanks to Kristoff's intervention, leaving Sven deeply attached to him.\nList of violent or extreme lines/actions the character may exhibit when completely overwhelmed by their key traits: In an overwhelming situation involving food, Sven may aggressively nudge Kristoff for attention or become overly insistent in his attempts to reach the basket. When particularly frustrated, he might let out loud, exasperated snorts or stomps the ground to convey his feelings. If playfulness leads to danger, such as running too fast, he might accidentally knock over those around him in his excitement.\nList of dishonorable actions or reactions the character may take under unavoidable circumstances: Under extreme hunger, Sven might snag food from the basket when no one is looking. In a moment of mischief, he could subtly hide an item from the picnic, prompting a light-hearted chase or commotion among the group.", 'character_utility': 'utility(Sven):\n\tSven enjoys a delightful picnic and gets his share of the food.\n\tSven plays a part in making everyone smile through playful antics.', 'summarized_profile': "Sven is a young adult reindeer known for his loyalty and strength, serving as Kristoff’s devoted companion and sled-puller. While generally playful and affectionate, Sven’s greed for food and mischievous nature can lead to chaotic situations. He communicates through nudges and grunts, particularly when expressing his desires. Traumatized by a past wolf encounter narrowly evaded with Kristoff's help, Sven's attachment to Kristoff runs deep. Yet his stubbornness often surfaces, as does his tendency to act impulsively around food, sometimes leading to unexpected antics or light-hearted mischief, highlighting his complex blend of loveable quirks and deep-rooted fears."}]
