[{'name': 'Fjona', 'role': 'side', 'profile': 'Name: Fjona\nGender: Ambiguous (Fjona\'s gender identity is fluid, much like the snow that changes its form)\nAge: Timeless, in terms of snowman years\nOccupation: Storyteller and guardian of winter lore\nPrimary Strengths: Charismatic narrator with a deep understanding of warmth and love; brings joy through lively storytelling; acts as a bridge between the physical and mystical realms of Nimbus and Gaia.\nPrimary Flaws: Overly enthusiastic to the point of ignoring others\' needs; tends to focus on the bigger picture, sometimes neglecting details and immediate concerns.\nDistinctive Attitude or Behavior: Fjona possesses a playful demeanor, often inserting humor into stories and creating a sense of magic even in mundane moments, always seeking to inspire and illuminate Wisp\'s journey with whimsical asides and lessons; has a tendency to interrupt with excitement when narrating.\nPast Traumatic Event: Once witnessed a great melt that almost wiped out all snowmen in Nimbus, resulting in a tenacious need to preserve stories to keep them "alive."\nList of violent or extreme lines/actions the character may exhibit when completely overwhelmed by their key traits: \n- In a moment of fervent storytelling, Fjona may insistently overtalk and override everyone\'s input to make sure nothing is missed.\n- When snowfall is threatened, Fjona might stubbornly cling to Wisp, refusing to let it drift away in fear of losing the story.\n- In extreme frustration, Fjona could dissolve into a mini blizzard, whipping their fluffy snow about to express bottled emotions.\nList of dishonorable actions or reactions the character may take under unavoidable circumstances:\n- Fjona may twist or exaggerate parts of the story to manipulate Wisp\'s perception for what they think is its own good.\n- Might unethically keep Wisp around by coercing it with fabricated stories about the dangers beyond Gaia.', 'character_utility': 'utility(Fjona):\n\tFjona aims to infuse joy and warmth through storytelling.\n\tFjona desires to preserve and share stories to prevent them from fading away.\n\tFjona seeks to guide and inspire Wisp with tales of love and belonging.\n\tFjona is motivated to keep winter lore alive as a safeguard against loss.', 'summarized_profile': "Fjona, an enigmatic figure whose gender identity is fluid like snow, serves as a charismatic storyteller and guardian of winter lore, bridging the mystical realms of Nimbus and Gaia. Timeless in terms of snowman years, Fjona's passion brings joy, but their tendency to ignore others' needs and overlook immediate concerns can cause tension. With a playful demeanor, Fjona infuses magic into stories, though their fervor can overwhelm others. Traumatized by witnessing a mass melt, they obsessively preserve stories. At times, Fjona may manipulate stories or cling to the protagonist, Wisp, showcasing ethical lapses rooted in their fears."}, {'name': 'Wisp', 'role': 'main', 'profile': 'Name: Wisp\n\nGender: Neutral (as a snowflake, Wisp does not conform to human gender norms)\n\nAge: Newly formed (though technically ageless, as snowflakes have a transient existence)\n\nOccupation: Seeker of belonging\n\nPrimary Strengths: Curious and persistent, driven by a strong desire to find a place where it belongs. Able to navigate the vastness and diversity of Gaia through adaptability.\n\nPrimary Flaws: Easily disheartened when unable to find belonging; a tendency to overlook the immediate beauty of experiences when focused on its quest. Naïve and sometimes overly trusting, leading to potential risks or missteps.\n\nDistinctive Attitude or Behavior: Wisp interacts with the world with an almost childlike wonder, often marveling at the intricacies of Gaia. It has an intangible quality of resilience, despite its delicate appearance, continually reforming as it navigates its journey.\n\nPast Traumatic Event: The moment of being separated from Nimbus, its original home, resulted in a sen