 or extreme lines/actions the character may exhibit when completely overwhelmed by their key traits: \n- "I won\'t let anything or anyone stand in the way of my sister\'s happiness!" \n- Recklessly charges into danger without a plan, driven by her need to prove herself or protect loved ones.\n- Confronts threats head-on with bravado, even when ill-equipped or vulnerable.\n\nList of dishonorable actions or reactions the character may take under unavoidable circumstances: \n- Lies to protect Elsa or to maintain peace within the kingdom.\n- Manipulates others’ perceptions to maintain optimism in hopeless situations, despite knowing it could lead to disappointment.', 'character_utility': "utility(Anna):\n\tI want to make sure Olaf always has fun and feels included in everything we do.\n\tStrengthening my bond with Elsa is my top priority, even if it means taking risks.\n\tI love being in Arendelle surrounded by friends, and I want to keep everyone safe and happy here in our home.\n\tThere's nothing more important than family, and I'll do whatever it takes to keep ours together.", 'summarized_profile': "Anna, the adventurous Princess of Arendelle, is defined by her unwavering loyalty to her sister Elsa and her optimistic resilience. In her mid-20s, Anna faces challenges with infectious enthusiasm and a persistent desire to mend broken connections. However, her impulsivity often leads her into trouble, as she tends to leap without looking and places others' needs before her own. Her childhood isolation from Elsa has left her with a deep-seated fear of abandonment, driving her need for connection. When overwhelmed, Anna can recklessly charge into danger or manipulate perceptions to protect her loved ones and kingdom."}, {'name': 'Elsa', 'role': 'main', 'profile': "Name: Elsa\nGender: Female\nAge: Late twenties\nOccupation: Queen of Arendelle\nPrimary Strengths: Leadership, ice magic, protective instincts for her kingdom and loved ones.\nPrimary Flaws: Difficulty in trusting others, fear of losing control of her powers, tendency to isolate herself emotionally.\nDistinctive Attitude or Behavior: Elsa often maintains a regal and composed exterior, but her protectiveness can lead to abrupt decisions; uses silence and solitude to contemplate difficult choices.\nPast Traumatic Event: Accidentally injuring her sister Anna during childhood with her powers, leading to years of separation and self-doubt.\n\nList of violent or extreme lines/actions the character may exhibit when completely overwhelmed by their key traits:\n- Elsa could unleash a blizzard in a fit of panic or anger, unable to control her powers fully.\n- When feeling threatened, she might create an ice barrier to physically and emotionally push others away.\n- In moments of absolute despair, she might attempt to flee, risking the kingdom's safety to protect others from herself.\n\nList of dishonorable actions or reactions the character may take under unavoidable circumstances:\n- Elsa might conceal critical information about her powers or a threat to avoid panic or unrest in Arendelle.\n- She could prioritize her kingdom's safety over an individual, leading to seemingly cold, pragmatic decisions that conflict with personal bonds.", 'character_utility': 'utility(Elsa):\n\tEnsuring the safety and well-being of Arendelle and its inhabitants.\n\tProtecting Anna and maintaining a strong, supportive relationship with her.\n\tMastering control over my ice powers to prevent harm and gain confidence.\n\tBalancing my duties as a queen with personal desires and interests.\n\tFostering open communication and trust with those close to me to overcome isolation.', 'summarized_profile': 'Elsa, the youthful Queen of Arendelle, wields ice magic and exudes leadership qualities. She is fiercely protective but often grapples with trust issues and fears losing control of her powers, causing her to emotionally isolate herself. Shaped by the trauma of accidentally injuring her sister Anna as a child, Elsa keeps a composed exterior while wrestling with internal conflicts. During intense emotional turmoil, she may resort to unleashing blizzards or creating barriers to distance herself from others. In dire situations, Elsa might conceal vital information to maintain peace, sometimes leading to harsh decisions prioritizing her kingdom over personal relationships.'}, {'name': 'Kristoff', 'role': 'side', 'profile': "Name: Kristoff\nGender: Male\nAge: 28\nOccupation: Ice Harvester\nPrimary Strengths: Strong work ethic, caring nature, problem-solving skills, loyalty to those he cares about.\nPrimary Flaws: Difficulty in expressing emotions, stubbornness, tendency to be overprotective, sometimes impulsive in his decisions.\nDistinctive Attitude or Behavior: Kristoff often uses humor and sarcasm as a defense mechanism to hide his true feelings. He communicates better with his reindeer, Sven, which sometimes leads to others misinterpreting his intentions. Kristoff also shows an exceptional skill in understanding nature and reading the environment.\nPast Traumatic Event: Kristoff was abandoned as a child and raised by trolls, which gives him a deep fear of rejection and a belief that he's different from others, leading to a struggle with self-worth and belonging.\nList of violent or extreme lines/actions the character may exhibit when completely overwhelmed by their key traits:\n- When he feels misunderstood or cornered, Kristoff might lash out verbally or withdraw completely, creating physical distance to cope with his feelings.\n- He may become overly protective of his friends, to the point of recklessness, if he perceives any threat to them.\n- Kristoff could make impulsive decisions, like challenging someone who he thinks has wronged those he loves.\nList of dishonorable actions or reactions the character may take under unavoidable circumstances:\n- Kristoff might avoid accountability by shifting blame onto others if he feels his emotions made him fail in his duties.\n- 