er her ice powers. Despite her composed demeanor, she battles perfectionism and anxiety, rooted in a childhood incident where she accidentally harmed her sister, Anna. This event spurred a fear of her abilities and led to years of self-imposed isolation. Elsa longs for emotional connection but often doubts her trust in others. Under extreme stress, her powers may manifest uncontrollably, leading to regretful actions. Her protective instincts can drive her to isolation or desperate measures to suppress her magic, highlighting her internal conflict.'}, {'name': 'Kristoff', 'role': 'side', 'profile': "Name: Kristoff Bjorgman\nGender: Male\nAge: Late 20s\nOccupation: Ice Harvester\n\nPrimary Strengths: \n- Physical strength and expertise in exploring mountainous terrains.\n- Deep sense of loyalty and care for those he loves, shown through his bond with Sven.\n\nPrimary Flaws:\n- Feels insecure and out of place amongst royals, leading to awkward social interactions.\n- Can be stubborn and resistant to change, especially when his independence is challenged.\n\nDistinctive Attitude or Behavior:\n- Tends to express himself through humor and sarcasm, sometimes as a defense mechanism.\n- Seeks validation and acceptance through acts of service or bravery, often going out of his way to help.\n\nPast Traumatic Event:\n- Grew up as an orphan, feeling lonely and disconnected, but found solace in the companionship of Sven.\n\nList of violent or extreme lines/actions the character may exhibit when completely overwhelmed by their key traits:\n- Might lash out with passive-aggressive remarks or sarcasm when he feels misunderstood or undervalued.\n- Could become uncharacteristically silent and withdraw when feeling severely insecure.\n- May take unnecessary physical risks to prove his worth or display his strength.\n\nList of dishonorable actions or reactions the character may take under unavoidable circumstances:\n- Might initially agree to deceptive or underhanded tactics if convince