uth, Fenrir harbors a distrust that fuels his obsession with power and control. In moments of desperation, he may lash out with verbal barbs, resort to intimidation, or even devolve into feral aggression. When confronted, he manipulates, spins lies, or feigns innocence to deflect blame and maintain his elusive command.'}, {'name': 'Nuna', 'role': 'side', 'profile': "Name: Nuna\nGender: Female\nAge: 70\nOccupation: Retired Herbalist\nPrimary Strengths: Resilience, Wisdom from experience, Unwavering hope\nPrimary Flaws: Stubbornness, Reluctance to accept help, Overprotectiveness towards Lira\nDistinctive Attitude or Behavior: Nuna is known for her gentle but firm demeanor that combines nurturing care with a no-nonsense attitude. She interacts with others by sharing stories of the past, often offering herbal remedies and advice gathered from years of living close to nature.\nPast Traumatic Event: Years ago, Nuna lost her husband to a harsh winter when they couldn't travel for medicinal supplies. This has left her with a fear of not being able to provide for and protect her loved ones in times of crisis.\nList of violent or extreme lines/actions the character may exhibit when completely overwhelmed by their key traits: \n- If Nuna feels her granddaughter is in immediate danger, she might confront a threat head-on, disregarding her own safety.\n- When extremely frustrated by persistent illness, she may lash out emotionally, insisting she doesn’t need any help.\n- Faced with relentless pressure, she might retreat into isolation to avoid being perceived as a burden.\n\nList of dishonorable actions or reactions the character may take under unavoidable circumstances:\n- Nuna might manipulate Lira's emotions by recounting family struggles in order to convince her to stay at the cottage rather than venture into the forest.\n- In a desperate bid to maintain her independence, Nuna could conceal the severity of her illness, preventing others from realizing the full extent of her 