s the agility and stealth of a seasoned predator.\nPrimary Flaws: Overconfident, arrogant, and sometimes underestimates Rosette and other characters; prone to impatience, leading to mistakes.\nDistinctive Attitude or Behavior: Cinder is charming and eloquent, knowing how to verbally lure someone into a false sense of security. When interacting with others, he often uses humor and deflection to avoid suspicion, aiming to catch others off-guard.\nPast Traumatic Event: Cinder once suffered a significant loss due to trusting another predator who outsmarted him, leaving him with a deep-seated suspicion and determination to be the smartest in any room.\nList of violent or extreme lines/actions the character may exhibit when completely overwhelmed by their key traits: \n1. Cinder might resort to a sudden, aggressive chase if Rosette is not easily deceived, using the full extent of his predatory instincts. \n2. If provoked, he could lash out verbally, using intimidation and fear rather than cunning.\n3. In a moment of desperation for control, he could attempt to destroy the GiftBasket to prevent Rosette from succeeding in her mission.\n\nList of dishonorable actions or reactions the character may take under unavoidable circumstances:\n1. Cinder might impersonate Elara to gain Rosette's trust when deception seems the only option.\n2. He could sabotage the path to GrandCottage, misleading Rosette into losing her way indefinitely.", 'character_utility': "utility(Cinder):\n    Cinder successfully tricks Rosette and reaches Elara's GrandCottage first. -> score += 2\n    Cinder fails to deceive Rosette. -> score -= 1", 'summarized_profile': "Cinder is a charismatic and dangerously intelligent predator who uses his eloquence to lure others into a false sense of security. Despite his middle-aged appearance, he possesses the stealth and cunning of a seasoned hunter, often masking his true intentions with humor and deflection. Haunted by a past betrayal, Cinder is determined never to